(a) the details of destinations and projects sanctioned in Himachal Pradesh under Swadesh Darshan 2.0 scheme and the Challenge Based Destination Development (CBDD) sub-scheme, during the last three years;
(b) the funds allocated and released for these projects in the State, year-wise;
(c) whether any proposals from the State under these schemes are pending with the Ministry and if so, the details and current status thereof; and
(d) the reasons for delay, if any, in completion of sanctioned projects in the State and the corrective measures being taken?

(a) whether Government is aware of the district-wise child sex ratio trends in Himachal Pradesh, particularly in districts such as Una and Hamirpur;
(b) if so, the details thereof along with the trend over the last five years, district-wise;
(c) whether Government proposes to intensify Beti Bachao Beti Padhao interventions in districts showing an adverse or stagnant sex ratio, and if so, the details and timeline thereof; and
(d) the steps taken/being taken by Government to strengthen enforcement of the PC&PNDT Act and promote convergence with State authorities to improve the child sex ratio in Himachal Pradesh?

(a) the credit-deposit ratio and priority sector lending achieved by the Himachal Pradesh Gramin Bank during the last three years;
(b) the quantum of credit extended by the Bank to horticulture, particularly Apple growers, and other hill-area farmers during the said period;
(c) whether Government has undertaken or proposes any recapitalisation, branch expansion or other strengthening measures for Regional Rural Banks operating in Himachal Pradesh; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to improve credit access for farmers in the hilly and remote areas of the State?

(a) the amount of unclaimed dividends and the number of shares belonging to investors from Himachal Pradesh transferred to the Investor Education and Protection Fund (IEPF), year-wise, during the last five years;
(b) the number of claims filed and the amount refunded to investors from the State under Form IEPF-5 during the said period;
(c) the steps taken by Government to create awareness among investors in the State, particularly in remote and hill districts, about the IEPF refund process; and
(d) whether Government proposes to further simplify the claim/refund procedure and if so, the details thereof?

