(a) the objectives of the 'Sahakar Se Samriddhi' initiative and the major steps being taken by Government under this initiative to strengthen the cooperative sector and make it self-reliant;
(b) the scheme-wise progress made so far in Himachal Pradesh under this initiative, including the financial, technical and institutional assistance provided to cooperative societies and the major outcomes achieved therefrom; and
(c) whether Government has implemented any special schemes or measures to strengthen the cooperative movement in the hilly, tribal and remote areas of Himachal Pradesh, including the promotion of new cooperative societies, capacity building, marketing, storage, processing, digitisation and financial inclusion, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the present status of physical and financial progress of the Bulk Drug Park being developed in Himachal Pradesh under the Scheme for Promotion of Bulk Drug Parks, component-wise;
(b) the funds allocated and released for the project, year-wise, since its approval;
(c) the expected timeline for completion and operationalisation of the Park; and
(d) the reasons for delay, if any, in completion of the common infrastructure facilities and the corrective measures being taken to expedite the same?

(a) whether pharmaceutical MSME clusters in the Baddi-Barotiwala-Nalagarh region of Himachal Pradesh have received support under the Scheme for Strengthening of Pharmaceutical Industry (SPI);
(b) if so, the number of units/clusters assisted and the quantum of financial assistance provided, year-wise;
(c) the nature of common infrastructure facilities created for improving productivity, quality and sustainability of these MSME clusters; and
(d) whether any proposals from Himachal Pradesh are currently pending under the Scheme and if so, the status thereof?

(a) whether the Central Government is aware of the status of heliport routes operationalized in the State of Himachal Pradesh under the Regional Connectivity Scheme (UDAN);
(b) if so, the route-wise details thereof along with their present operational status and the Viability Gap Funding (VGF) sanctioned and disbursed during the last three years;
(c) whether any UDAN heliport routes proposed/awarded for the State of Himachal Pradesh have been discontinued or remain non-operational, and if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps being taken by the Central Government to enhance heliport connectivity under UDAN in the hill districts of the State?

(a) whether Government is aware of frequent flight cancellations/diversions at airports in the State of Himachal Pradesh on account of fog and adverse weather conditions, particularly during winter months;
(b) if so, the current status of installation of Instrument Landing System (ILS)/RNAV or other all-weather landing aids at Kangra (Gaggal), Kullu (Bhuntar) and Shimla airports, airport-wise;
(c) the funds allocated and released for installation/upgradation of such landing technology during the last three years, year-wise; and
(d) the timeline by when installation of all-weather landing aids at the remaining airports is likely to be completed?

(a) the number of export infrastructure projects, including cold-chain and logistics facilities, sanctioned for Himachal Pradesh under the Trade Infrastructure for Export Scheme (TIES) during the last five years;
(b) the funds allocated and released for such projects in Himachal Pradesh, year-wise;
(c) whether any proposal(s) from Himachal Pradesh under TIES is/are pending, if so, the details and current status thereof; and
(d) the reasons for delay, if any and the corrective measures being taken?

(a) whether Government has commissioned the X-Band Doppler Weather Radar sanctioned for Lahaul and Spiti district since its procurement was announced and if so, the date of its commissioning;
(b) if not, the details thereof along with the revised timeline for commissioning;
(c) whether Government proposes to extend similar dedicated radar or Automatic Weather Station coverage to Kinnaur and other cloudburst-affected districts of Himachal Pradesh under Mission Mausam and if so, the details and timeline thereof; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to close the monitoring gap in remote hill blocks where the nearest weather station to recent disaster sites has been reported to be several kilometres away?

(a) whether any scheme or programme has been formulated for convergence of Panchayati Raj Institutions with the National Action Plan for Drug Demand Reduction (NAPDDR) for grassroots-level drug awareness in villages, particularly in Himachal Pradesh;
(b) if so, the number of Gram Panchayats in Himachal Pradesh covered under such convergence and the funds allocated and released therefor, year-wise, during the last three years;
(c) whether any proposal(s) from Himachal Pradesh for expansion of such Panchayat-level initiatives is/are pending; and
(d) the reasons for delay, if any, in implementation of such proposals and the corrective measures being taken?

(a) the  cumulative account enrolment under the Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) and Jan Suraksha Schemes, State-wise and gender-wise;
(b) the total quantum of loans disbursed under the MUDRA scheme, along with category-wise details for SC/ST/OBC and women borrowers and the status of sanctions under the ‘Tarun Plus’ category; and
(c) the current NPA position under the scheme and the trend during the last three financial years?

(a) the year-wise reduction in imports of key technical-grade pesticides, dyes and chemical intermediates since 2014, along with the major reasons therefor;
(b) the current status of the proposed Production-Linked Incentive (PLI) framework aimed at promoting domestic feedstock manufacturing, including the progress made so far and the likely timeline for its implementation; and
(c) whether Government has undertaken digital safety compliance audits in units handling hazardous chemicals with a view to reducing industrial accidents, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the key provisions made under the AYUSH Drug Quality and Production Enhancement Scheme to ensure quality of AYUSH medicines and to enhance production capacity in the country;
(b) the details of AYUSH drug manufacturing units established/upgraded under the said scheme across various States, particularly in Himachal Pradesh;
(c) whether Government has developed any specific mechanism for standardisation, testing and certification of AYUSH medicines; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government is aware of the limited heliport infrastructure currently available in the hill State of Himachal Pradesh;
(b) if so, the number of operational heliports in the State along with their location-wise details;
(c) whether Government proposes to construct new heliports in the State of Himachal Pradesh and if so, the location-wise details, present status and timeline thereof; and
(d) the steps taken/being taken by Government to expand heliport infrastructure in the State, including the funds allocated and released, as well as those earmarked for the future, year-wise?

(a) whether Government is aware of the present status of the land acquisition/transfer process required for expansion of airport infrastructure at Kangra (Gaggal) and Kullu (Bhuntar) airports in the State of Himachal Pradesh;
(b) if so, the details thereof along with the funds allocated and released, if any, towards land acquisition/compensation for these projects during the last three years, year-wise;
(c) whether the Central Government proposes to expedite coordination with the State Government to complete the pending land acquisition process and if so, the details and timeline thereof; and
(d) the steps taken/being taken by Government to ensure timely completion of expansion works at these airports?

(a) the number of farmers and area brought under the National Mission on Natural Farming (NMNF), State/UT-wise, particularly for Himachal Pradesh, during the last three years;
(b) the funds allocated and released to Himachal Pradesh under the Mission, year-wise;
(c) whether any proposal(s) from Himachal Pradesh for expansion of natural farming clusters or training infrastructure is/are pending with Government, if so, the details and current status thereof; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to encourage wider adoption of natural farming practices among hill-State farmers, given the terrain and input-cost challenges specific to such States?

(a) whether the Ministry has commissioned or is in the process of commissioning an architecture and heritage planning consultancy covering the Kinnaur and Lahaul & Spiti districts of Himachal Pradesh;
(b) the scope, objectives and timeline of this consultancy;
(c) whether local stakeholders, monasteries and community representatives in these districts have been consulted as part of this exercise; and
(d) the expected outcomes of this consultancy for the preservation of Buddhist and Tibetan heritage in the region?

(a) the details of Amended BharatNet Programme (ABP) being implemented in Himachal Pradesh under the Digital Bharat Nidhi, including the total project cost allocated for the State;
(b) the Gram Panchayat-wise and block-wise targets fixed for last-mile Fibre-to-the-Home (FTTH) connectivity to Government institutions such as schools, health centres and anganwadis in the State, along with progress achieved, so far;
(c) the funds released till date against the sanctioned allocation for Himachal Pradesh, year-wise; and
(d) the timeline by which the programme is expected to be completed across all Gram Panchayats of the State?

(a) the number of villages identified in Himachal Pradesh under the Vibrant Villages Programme, district-wise and the current status of implementation of road connectivity, power supply, healthcare, communication network and drinking water facilities in these villages;
(b) the funds allocated and released for Himachal Pradesh under the Programme, year-wise, during the last three years;
(c) whether any Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) or proposals from Himachal Pradesh under the Programme are pending with Government and if so, the details and current status thereof; and
(d) the reasons for delay, if any, in completion of identified works and the corrective measures being taken?

(a) the details of school/college-level drug awareness and substance abuse prevention programmes currently being implemented, particularly in Himachal Pradesh, during the last three years;
(b) the funds allocated and released for such programmes in Himachal Pradesh, year-wise;
(c) whether any proposal(s) from Himachal Pradesh for expansion of such awareness programmes, including collaboration with NCERT/CBSE or the Narcotics Control Bureau, is/are pending; and
(d) the reasons for delay, if any, in implementation of such programmes and the corrective measures being taken?

(a) the number of Government hospital-based drug de-addiction centres/units currently functional in Himachal Pradesh under the National Mental Health Programme or any other Central scheme, district-wise;
(b) the funds allocated and released for setting up and running such de-addiction centres/units in Himachal Pradesh, during the last three years, year-wise;
(c) whether any proposal(s) from Himachal Pradesh for setting up new de-addiction units or upgrading existing ones is/are pending with Government; and
(d) the reasons for delay, if any, in operationalising/upgrading such centres and the corrective measures being taken?

(a) whether Government is aware of the shortage of healthcare infrastructure and specialist availability in remote tribal and border blocks of Himachal Pradesh such as Kinnaur, Lahaul-Spiti, Pangi and Bharmour;
(b) if so, the details of Primary Health Centres (PHCs), Community Health Centres (CHCs)and specialist positions currently functional versus sanctioned in these areas;
(c) whether Government proposes to expand telemedicine and mobile health unit coverage in these areas, and if so, the details and timeline thereof; and
(d) the steps taken or being taken by Government to ensure adequate healthcare access for tribal and border populations in Himachal Pradesh?

(a) whether Government is aware of present status of infrastructure and air connectivity at existing airports in Himachal Pradesh, namely Kangra (Gaggal), Kullu (Bhuntar) and Shimla;
(b) if so, the details thereof along with the expansion/modernization plans approved or under progress at these airports, including runway extension at Shimla and increase in flight frequency/operational hours;
(c) whether Government proposes to expedite these projects, and if so, the estimated cost and timeline thereof, airport-wise; and
(d) steps taken/being taken by Government to improve air connectivity to Himachal Pradesh, and expected impact of these projects on tourism and regional development in the State?

(a) whether there is any provision of reservation for Scheduled Castes (SC), Scheduled Tribes (ST) and Other Backward Classes (OBC) in the appointment of judges in various courts of the country such as the Supreme Court, High Courts, District and Sessions Courts etc.;
(b) if so, the court-wise percentage of reservation prescribed for these categories;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) whether Government is considering introducing any policy or special measures to enhance social diversity and representation of these categories in the judiciary?

(a) whether reservation provisions for Scheduled Castes (SC), Scheduled Tribes (ST) and Other Backward Classes (OBC) are being implemented in various departments/attached institutions under the Ministry;
(b) if so, the category-wise/institution-wise details regarding the number of posts reserved for SC, ST and OBC categories in these institutions, the posts filled and those remaining vacant;
(c) whether Government is considering implementing any special drive or policy to expedite the filling of posts reserved for these categories; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and the progress made in this direction, so far?

(a) how many National Highway projects have been approved in Himachal Pradesh at present and how many are pending;
(b) what amount has been spent on these projects during the last three years, project-wise and year-wise, details thereof; and
(c) what steps Government is taking to complete the pending projects at the earliest?

(a) manner in which the dedicated Hydrogen Production Plant at Jind successfully supported the zero-emission refueling requirements for the eight-coach rakes;
(b) the positive environmental findings regarding the elimination of carbon emissions during the 20-km Jind-Lalit Khera test stretch;
(c) whether the Ministry is on track to operationalise the Jind-Sonipat hydrogen circuit for regular passenger service by mid-2026;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) manner in which the energy efficiency of one kilogram of hydrogen compares to traditional diesel traction in these heritage circuit trials?

(a) the number of public EV charging stations approved and made operational under the Faster Adoption and Manufacturing of Hybrid and Electric Vehicles (FAME-II) scheme, including Mahrashtra and Uttar Pradesh;
(b) whether the charging stations are evenly distributed across various districts of the States;
(c) if so, the details of such distribution, district-wise;
(d) whether the utilization rate of the installed EV chargers in the States have been assessed;
(e) if so, the details of the results of such assessment;
(f) whether interoperability standards are being implemented in the charging network; and
(g) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of beneficiaries under the PMGKAY across the country and specifically in Himachal Pradesh;
(b) the quantity of foodgrains distributed under the scheme and the expenditure incurred thereon; and
(c) whether Government decided any special provisions for States like Himachal Pradesh, which are predominantly hilly, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total quantity and value of exports of chemicals and fertilizers from the country during the last three years and Himachal Pradesh’s share therein, year-wise;
(b) whether Government has implemented any special policy or incentive package to promote exports in the chemicals and fertilizers sector and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of special steps taken to promote exports from industrial areas/pharmaceutical and chemical units located in Himachal Pradesh; and
(d) the concrete measures proposed to be taken by Government in future to enhance exports in the chemicals and fertilizers sector in the country, including Himachal Pradesh?

(a) whether Government is promoting metro rail expansion in accordance with the National Urban Transport Policy (NUTP), 2025;
(b) if so, the details of new metro projects approved during the last three years and their present status;
(c) whether there is any plan to implement systems such as Light Metro, Metro Neo and Metro Lite in Tier-II cities; and
(d) whether it is proposed to adopt the PPP model or other innovative approaches in metro rail projects?

(a) the rules/guidelines presently in force for plastic waste management in the country and the status of their effective implementation;
(b) the details of processes being adopted for collection, segregation, processing and recycling of plastic waste and the role of States/local bodies therein;
(c) the status of compliance with the ban on single-use plastic and the penal action taken so far in cases of violations; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to promote recycling and innovation for utilisation of plastic waste in energy generation, road construction and other applications?

(a) the schemes currently being implemented by the Central Government across the country, particularly in Himachal Pradesh, for the welfare, nutrition, health and safety of women and children;
(b) the year-wise amount allocated and expenditure incurred for Himachal Pradesh under these schemes during the last three years;
(c) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the effectiveness of schemes related to Anganwadi services, maternal nutrition, prevention of child malnutrition and women’s safety in the State; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has approved the second phase of the Vibrant Villages Programme (VVP-II) for the comprehensive development of villages located along international borders;
(b) the total financial outlay, duration of the Programme and the number of villages, blocks, States and Union Territories proposed to be covered under Phase-II;
(c) the provisions made under the Programme for development of infrastructure, road and digital connectivity, livelihood generation, tourism and social amenities; and
(d) whether villages in Himachal Pradesh and other border States have been identified under Phase-II and if so, the State-wise details thereof?

(a) the details of Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) monitoring framework and the reporting requirements for companies implemented through the CSR-2 filing module on the portal of the Ministry;
(b) the number of companies that have reported CSR expenditure and unspent amounts during the last three years, year-wise;
(c) the mechanisms to monitor the transfer of unspent CSR funds to the prescribed accounts or funds; and
(d) whether any review or impact assessment has been conducted on CSR compliance and transparency, if so, the key findings thereof?

(a) the details of the financial outlay and the year-wise allocation proposed under the Scheme;
(b) the steps proposed for creation of accredited clinical trial sites across the country and the expected outcomes thereof;
(c) the initiatives taken to strengthen the regulatory framework, including capacity enhancement of Central Drugs Standard Control Organisation (CDSCO) for faster approval of biologics and biosimilars; and
(d) the manner in which the Scheme is expected to reduce import dependence and enhance India’s share in the global biopharmaceutical market?

(a) the details of projects sanctioned and funds released under the Central Sector Scheme on Conservation, Development and Sustainable Management of Medicinal Plants during the last five years, State-wise;
(b) the measurable impact of this scheme on the area expansion and cultivation of medicinal plants across the country including Jharkhand and Haryana;
(c) the steps taken for in-situ and ex-situ conservation of rare, endangered and threatened medicinal species;
(d) the effectiveness of the e-Charak mobile application in improving market access and price transparency for medicinal plant growers; and
(e) whether there is any monitoring mechanism to track survival rate, productivity and income enhancement of medicinal plant cultivators?

(a) the specific non-fossil fuel electricity capacity target India achieved nearly five years ahead of the scheduled timeline;
(b) the manner in which the share of non-fossil fuels in the total installed power generation capacity has changed between 2014 and December 2025;
(c) whether Government has identified specific measures to address the challenges of climate change through energy transition initiatives; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, and by when Government is likely to achieve the next major milestone in expanding renewable energy capacity?

(a) whether Government has any proposal under consideration for extension of Amb Anduara railway line in Himachal Pradesh, if so, present status thereof, estimated cost and likely time-frame for its completion;
(b) expected timeline for completion of new Bilaspur railway line and estimated cost involved in completing the same;
(c) present status of Bilaspur–Mandi–Leh railway line project and whether any survey is being conducted for this project, if so, the estimated cost thereof; and
(d) whether Government is considering conversion of Pathankot–Joginder Nagar narrow gauge railway line into broad gauge, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the year-wise amount of funds allocated by the Central Government to Himachal Pradesh under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) during the last three years;
(b) the actual amount of funds utilized in Himachal Pradesh under the said scheme during the above period, the amount of funds that remained unutilized and lapsed, if any, along with component-wise details thereof; and
(c) the total number of Utilization Certificates submitted by Government of Himachal Pradesh to the Central Government so far under the said scheme, the number of certificates pending, along with phase-wise details thereof?

(a) the steps taken by Government to strengthen and expand the mobile network in the country and the budget allocated for this purpose;
(b) whether Government is considering to provide mobile network connectivity in remote areas of Himachal Pradesh where such facilities are still unavailable; and
(c) whether any provision has been made in the budget to maintain and expand mobile network there, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the purposes for which radiation technologies are being used in the medical and health sector in the country, including Himachal Pradesh;
(b) the details of radiopharmaceutical products developed/launched by the Department during the last three years till date and which of these products are available in Himachal Pradesh;
(c) whether Government has taken any steps for indigenisation and commercialisation of radiopharmaceutical products; and
(d) if so, the details thereof with specific reference to Himachal Pradesh?

(a) the year-wise details of the number of youth who have been provided skill training under the Skill India Mission in the country, including Himachal Pradesh, during the last three years and the current year and out of these, how many have obtained employment/self-employment after training;
(b) the special training programmes centre and industry-partnership-based initiatives being implemented for skill development keeping in view the specific requirements of the hilly, rural and tribal areas of Himachal Pradesh; and
(c) the mechanism adopted by Government for monitoring and evaluation of the quality of skill training, employment linkage and outcomes under Skill India in Himachal Pradesh?

(a) the year-wise amount of funds allocated by the Central Government to Himachal Pradesh during the last three years under various Central education-related schemes;
(b) the amount actually utilized and the amount lapsed during the said period under these schemes in Himachal Pradesh, along with scheme-wise details thereof;
(c) the number of Utilization Certificates submitted so far by Government of Himachal Pradesh to the Central Government under these schemes and the number pending, scheme-wise; and
(d) the steps taken by the Central Government to ensure proper and timely utilization of funds allocated under education schemes in the State?

(a) the year-wise amount of funds allocated by the Central Government to Himachal Pradesh during the last three years under various Central Government health schemes;
(b) out of the above, how much amount has actually been utilised in Himachal Pradesh during the said period and how much amount has lapsed, along with scheme-wise details;
(c) the number of Utilisation Certificates submitted so far by Government of Himachal Pradesh to the Central Government and the number pending, along with scheme-wise details; and
(d) the steps being taken by the Central Government to ensure proper and timely utilisation of the funds allocated under health schemes in the State?

(a) percentage of ethanol blending achieved so far under the Ethanol Blended Petrol (EBP) Programme in the country and the year-wise achievements;
(b) the quantity of ethanol supplied during the last three years in the country, State-wise, including Himachal Pradesh;
(c) achievements attained so far from ethanol blending in terms of foreign exchange savings, reduction in crude oil imports, increase in farmers’ income and environmental benefits; and
(d) whether Government is taking any additional steps to achieve the stipulated ethanol blending target by 2025–26 by enhancing production capacity, promoting distillery projects and strengthening the supply chain, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the provisions made under the PM E-DRIVE scheme to promote electric mobility in the country, particularly in Himachal Pradesh;
(b) the number of electric vehicles, charging stations and related infrastructure sanctioned/established in Himachal Pradesh under the said scheme so far;
(c) the central financial assistance provided to Himachal Pradesh under this scheme during the last three years, the year-wise details thereof; and
(d) whether any special policy or additional assistance has been provided for promoting electric vehicles in the hilly and remote areas of the State?

(a) the schemes/programmes currently being implemented by Government to promote tourism and strengthen the tourism-based economy in Himachal Pradesh;
(b) the concrete steps taken by Government to enhance tourism infrastructure, homestays, adventure tourism, religious/eco-tourism and local employment generation in the State; and
(c) whether any new special scheme has been proposed to encourage rural tourism and develop tourist destinations/villages that are not featuring prominently on the tourism map and  if so, the details thereof along with the proposed budget for the State?

(a) the objectives and key components of the scheme to provide support to startups and nascent entrepreneurs in the country under the Pradhan Mantri Skilling and Employability Transformation through Upgraded ITIs (PM-SETU) initiative, especially in Himachal Pradesh;
(b) the number of youths/startups/entrepreneurs in Himachal Pradesh who have received skill training, mentorship and financial support so far under this initiative and the district-wise details thereof;
(c) whether this initiative has been coordinated with Skill India, Startup India and other Central/State-level entrepreneurship schemes in the State; and
(d) if so, its impact on employment generation, promotion of self-employment and sustainability of startups in Himachal Pradesh?

(a) the provisions made under the "One Nation, One Map" initiative to prepare integrated digital maps at the panchayat level for land records, asset mapping and village infrastructure;
(b) the current status of digital mapping and geo-referencing at the panchayat level in the country, particularly in Himachal Pradesh, under this initiative;
(c) whether the initiative has been linked to the Survey of Villages Abadi and Mapping with Improvised Technology in Village Areas (SVAMITVA) scheme and the e-Gram Swaraj platform; and
(d) if so, the impact this had on the planning process, asset management and transparency of the Panchayats?

(a) the major digital services being provided to companies and Limited Liability Partnerships (LLPs) registered in the State of Himachal Pradesh through e-governance initiatives;
(b) the increase recorded during the last three years in the utilisation of e-governance–based corporate services in the State of Himachal Pradesh; and
(c) the specific steps taken by Government to strengthen digital compliance, technical support and grievance redressal mechanisms in the State?

(a) schemes currently being implemented in the country to provide financial assistance and loans to Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs);
(b) the number of MSMEs in the country and in the State of Himachal Pradesh that have been provided loans/financial assistance under these schemes during the last three years and the amount disbursed in this regard, year-wise the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government plans to simplify the loan process for MSMEs in future, offer concessions in interest rates and increase credit guarantee coverage, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total amount allocated and spent under Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) funds in the State of Himachal Pradesh by Public Sector Undertakings and other central public sector undertakings during the last three years, year-wise and undertaking-wise details thereof;
(b) the areas where the CSR fund has been utilized in the State during this period, and the district-wise details thereof; and
(c) whether Government has established any monitoring and evaluation mechanism to ensure that the CSR fund in the State is being used transparently, effectively, and in accordance with local needs and if so, the details thereof?

(a) special incentives/facilities that are being provided under the Foreign Trade Policy to promote exports from the State of Himachal Pradesh at present;
